Source: flickos-greeter
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-installsysusers
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-greeter
Architecture: all
# flickos-session and the default wallpaper are in flickos-settings 1.12;
# flickos-session-plain, which /etc/greetd/environments offers below it (every
# line of that file is a session in gtkgreet's list, so it has no comments),
# in 1.42, and the plain session's folder comes from flickos-layouts 1.47.
Depends: greetd,
         gtkgreet,
         cage,
         arc-theme,
         flickos-settings (>= 1.42),
         flickos-layouts (>= 1.47),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: FlickOS graphical login screen
 Sets up greetd with gtkgreet (in the cage kiosk compositor) as the login
 screen of installed FlickOS systems, in the Arc-Dark colors and with the
 system keyboard layout. It starts the FlickOS session (flickos-session).
 .
 Members of the group "autologin" are logged in automatically (the first
 one, if there are several). The installer adds the user to it when
 "Log in automatically" is chosen.
 .
 The login screen does not run in the live session, which keeps its
 automatic login on tty1.
